 C/STAR:,NAME,
C===========================================================
C C/STAR - store into a non-simple packed field addressed through a
C pointer.
C
C   Entry:  ACC = the field's shift amount (untagged plain integer)
C           [SP-1] = the value to store
C           M11 = address of the width-specific table (C/01/C/02/C/03/
C                 C/04/C/06/C/07, picked by work.p2c at compile time --
C                 see libc/c_01.madlen)
C           M14 = address of the word(s) containing the field, set by
C                 setAddrTo(14)
C           M13 = return link
C
C Shares C/LDAR/C/RR's prologue (through the second ,ATI,10); diverges
C after that into the store-specific merge of the new value with the
C surrounding word(s).  This is a verbatim port of the Pascal runtime's
C P/STAR (paslib/p_star.dtran); the width-table format it reads via M11
C is not independently understood beyond the shape documented at
C c_01.madlen.  The fixpoint check and full test suite verify it.
C===========================================================
                ,NTR ,3
            1   ,AOX ,11B
           15   ,ATX ,1
           11   ,A*X ,
                ,ATI ,10
           10   ,J+M ,14
           11   ,A*X ,1
                ,YTA ,100B
           15   ,X-A ,1
                ,ATI ,10
           15   ,XTA ,-1
           11   ,WTC ,3
           10   ,ASX ,
           15   ,ATX ,-1
           14   ,AEX ,
           11   ,WTC ,4
           10   ,AAX ,
           15   ,AEX ,
           14   ,ATX ,
           13   ,UJ  ,
                ,END ,
